;; The lexer table starts at 31,457,280: {pointer,length,kind,padding}, 16 bytes.
;; Formatting scratch occupies 31,588,352..31,719,424. A failed parse publishes
;; an error view there; callers must consume it before the next parse_type call.
;; Grammar calls use bounded Wasm call-stack recursion, never linear-memory
;; stack frames or an allocator. Error code zero means success throughout.
